# Events
Every stdout line in JSON mode is a JSON object with type and one invocation run_id UUID. Human progress is stderr. scan reports files/bytes; part reports path/part/bytes/resumed; retry reports attempt/delay_ms; file reports validated receipt; complete reports files/bytes/uploaded_bytes/resumed_bytes.
Confirmed unique bytes exclude retransmission traffic. A completed-file fast path counts all its bytes as resumed; a partial session counts validated saved parts as resumed and new confirmations as uploaded. These paths are mutually exclusive.
The public schema does not include wire_bytes. Development probes measure it, but exposing it is deferred. Do not copy raw response bodies or authorization into events.
Example:
{"type":"scan","run_id":"d24b3c66-72c9-4efe-9d43-8ac7000f4db2","files":1,"bytes":9437291}
{"type":"retry","run_id":"d24b3c66-72c9-4efe-9d43-8ac7000f4db2","path":"archive.bin","part":2,"attempt":1,"delay_ms":347}
{"type":"complete","run_id":"d24b3c66-72c9-4efe-9d43-8ac7000f4db2","files":1,"bytes":9437291,"uploaded_bytes":9437291,"resumed_bytes":0}
Unknown future event types may be ignored by consumers. Initial parse failures may precede discovery of --json; those failures currently use stderr plain text.

